/**
 * How Embracing waves in a circle (`maru-ni-daki-nami`) is constructed, in a line in each language: the text a crest's card shows beside its steps.
 * It is here, not on the crest's record, so that the manifest stays small; `crestConstruction()` loads it.
 *
 * @example
 * ```ts no-run
 * import { description } from "@johnmorrisdotca/kamon-crests/steps/maru-ni-daki-nami";
 *
 * console.log(description.en.length > 30, description.ja.endsWith("。")); // true true
 * ```
 */
const description: { en: string; ja: string } = {"en":"A thin ring, and inside it two waves that rise on either side and curl in towards each other. Each wave is a mass of ink, and the book's own brush lines are the white lines in it, their edges arcs of circles struck in full and ruled lines. Where a line runs into the ring in the book, a narrow gap between two ruled lines carries its white on to the white inside the ring. The left wave is drawn first; the right wave is the same mirrored, built where it stands, and the two overlap a little on the middle so that no seam shows.","ja":"細い輪の中に、左右から立ち上がって中へ巻き込む二つの波を収めます。波は墨のかたまりで、本に描かれた筆の線が、その中の白い線になります。白い線のふちは、全部の円を描いたうえで、その弧と直線で作図します。本で線が輪までのびているところは、二本の直線の間の細いすき間で、白を輪の内側の白までつなぎます。先に左の波を作図し、右の波は同じものを左右反転させて、その場で作図します。真ん中では少し重ねて、継ぎ目が出ないようにします。"};

export default construction;
export { construction, description };
